# A subject of two blanks and 988 letters, 990 bytes.  After "Subject: " it
# would make a line of 999, so the value folds at the colon.  The line after
# the fold begins with the blank after the colon, as without a fold
# (subject-blanks), and has the value's two blanks after it, 991 bytes in
# all.  A value of 998 bytes would not fit that way: its line has the
# value's blanks and not the one after the colon (subject-leading-blanks).
mode=accept
tls=none
form=(From=alice@example.com To=bob@example.net Body=$'Hi\n' User=alice Password=secret
      Subject="$(printf ' %.0s' $(seq 2))$(printf 'N%.0s' $(seq 988))")
